    {
      "CVE": "CVE-2026-12244",
      "Description": "If NSD is configured as secondary for a zone, the primary of that zone can crash NSD with an AXFR containing a DNS message with a special crafted SVCB RR with an rdata size of 65512, that let's an (uint16_t) variable that is used to allocate space needed for the RR wrap (because total size \u003e 65535), causing a heap overflow. The attacker can perform a controlled (RCE class) head write of up to 65509 bytes",
      "Threats": [
        {
          "Type": "Impact",
          "Severity": "moderate"
        }
      ],
      "References": [
